# FEX x86 guest rootfs — the userspace an emulated x86/x86_64 *Linux* binary sees.
#
# FEX does not chroot: it overlays this image as the guest's `/`, so an x86 ELF finds x86 copies
# of libc, libstdc++, the GL/Vulkan loaders and so on, while the host thunks forward the graphics
# and audio calls back out to the real arm64 drivers. Without a rootfs an x86 binary has no
# libraries at all and dies at the dynamic loader.
#
# ARCH, not Fedora. Games shipped for Linux target the SteamOS userspace, which is Arch-derived,
# so the Arch guest rootfs is the closest match to what a Linux game expects to link against. It
# also matches the sysroot the guest thunks are compiled against (packages/fex-emu/PKGBUILD).
#
# NOTE: the Windows-game path does NOT use this file. Proton carries its own WoW64 FEX, which
# translates x86 Windows code and never needs a Linux guest rootfs (its bundled FEX config sets
# neither RootFS nor ThunksDB). This image exists solely for native x86 Linux ELFs.
#
# erofs, not squashfs: upstream publishes both. The .ero is ~1.9G against ~1.1G for the .sqsh,
# but it is random-access friendly, which matters for a filesystem the emulator reads on every
# library resolution. FEXServer picks the mount helper from the container type — `erofsfuse` for
# this file (SquashFS.cpp), which is why fex-emu hard-depends on it. Both the image and the
# helper must agree; swapping to .sqsh means depending on squashfuse instead.
#
# Raw file, not an archive: `kind: file` copies it verbatim to `dest` (no tar, no strip).
#
# The upstream index (https://rootfs.fex-emu.gg/RootFS_links.json) publishes an xxhash, not a
# sha256 — the hash below was computed from the downloaded artifact.
#
# Fields: see packages/inputplumber/prebuilt.pin for the base set; this pin adds
#   kind   -> `file` (copy verbatim) or `tar` (extract; the default)
#   dest   -> absolute path in the rootfs. For `file`, the full destination FILE path.
#
# To bump: pick a newer dated build from RootFS_links.json, then set version + url + sha256
# together (the filename stays ArchLinux.ero, so Config.json needs no change).
name: fex-rootfs
version: 2026-01-08
url: https://rootfs.fex-emu.gg/ArchLinux/2026-01-08/ArchLinux.ero
sha256: 231febb39c636feb89426a21aca3b2ceb121645dbaac7858431d1b7bc7dfde95
kind: file
dest: /usr/share/fex-emu/RootFS/ArchLinux.ero
